# Bible Challenge Arena - Apache configuration for KSWEB / Apache / localhost
# Place this whole project folder inside your web server's document root,
# e.g. KSWEB htdocs/biblegame/, then visit http://PHONE-IP:8000/biblegame/

# Serve index.html automatically when a directory is requested
DirectoryIndex index.html

# Hide directory listings
Options -Indexes

# CORS is handled per-request in api/db.php's corsOrigin() (restricted to an
# allow-list rather than "*", now that this runs on a public domain instead
# of LAN-only) - this block is deliberately NOT setting
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin here so PHP's own header() call is the only
# one that applies (Apache would otherwise send both, and having two
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin headers on one response is invalid/unreliable
# across browsers).

# NOTE: We deliberately do NOT force a PHP SetHandler here. KSWEB (and most
# Apache+PHP builds) already register .php files with their own handler
# (mod_php or PHP-FPM via a proxy handler whose name we cannot predict).
# Overriding it with the wrong handler name causes PHP files to either 500
# or be served as plain text/source instead of being executed, which looks
# to the app like "Could not reach the host server" even though Apache did
# respond. If your KSWEB build truly does not execute .php automatically,
# enable PHP support in the KSWEB app settings instead of patching this file.

# Game data lives in MySQL (see api/db.php for connection settings), not a
# SQLite file under this document root. The database/ folder only holds a
# static import seed file and generated export dumps; database/.htaccess
# blocks direct web access to both, so they can't be fetched by URL.
